 "thread": "waocYzH7NqE",
 "subject": "How could one post to a wordpress blog, like the googleVis package",
 "messages_listed": 2,
 "last_activity": "2013-03-06T16:38:49Z",
 "messages": [
  {
   "id": "yP1L-CTI0qAJ",
   "from": "brendan dornan",
   "author": "d8d878a122444ca0",
   "date": "2013-03-05T16:31:05Z",
   "subject": "How could one post to a wordpress blog, like the googleVis package",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:16px;line-height:24px\">Great package, thanks for building. Is it possible to render interactive charts in self-hosted blog posts like one can with the googleVis + R package?</span></h1><h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><br></h1><h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><a href=\"https://code.google.com/p/google-motion-charts-with-r/wiki/UsingWordPress\" style=\"font-size:16px;line-height:24px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://code.google.com/p/google-motion-charts-with-r/wiki/UsingWordPress&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675308000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2o7IOo4_9EKEP-Lke0_aT8\">Using googleVis output with WordPress</a><br></h1><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://wordpress.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wordpress.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675308000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0hj9LLvVReEPRYj2GXNeby\">WordPress</a> is a popular web software for creating websites and blogs. Here we give some tips about the usage with googleVis output.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">By default WordPress does not allow JavaScript code (and hence googleVis output) to be inserted into a page. However, additional plugins allow us to extend the functions of WordPress.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">One option of embedding JavaScript code inside a WordPress post is to use the <a href=\"http://wordpress.org/extend/plugins/custom-fields-shortcode\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wordpress.org/extend/plugins/custom-fields-shortcode&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675308000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2ECUGoNXBxMZHRj9Lih1mk\">&quot;custom fields shortcode&quot;</a> plugin. This plugin allows you to create a custom field for the googleVis code, which can be referred to in your article.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Suppose you created a motion chart in R:</p><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span>M </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span> gvisMotionChart</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Fruits</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Fruit&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Year&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span><br>                     options</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span>list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>width</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">400</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> height</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">370</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></pre><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Copy the chart code, e.g. from</p><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">print</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>M</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;chart&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></pre><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">and paste it into the value text area of a custom field in WordPress, e.g. with instance name <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">Fruits</tt>. To include the motion chart into your article add <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">[cf]Fruits[/cf]</tt> into the post, see the figure below for an illustration. For more details see also the <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googleVis/vignettes/googleVis.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googleVis/vignettes/googleVis.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675308000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3eYap9IckAKTPV_qptqcYe\">vignette</a>.</p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "zphdu1dUtB0J",
   "from": "Alex Brown",
   "author": "c8fe4075ec631c03",
   "date": "2013-03-06T16:38:49Z",
   "subject": "Re: How could one post to a wordpress blog, like the googleVis package",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "With google VIS the server side providing the data is always there and hosted by a third party.<div><br></div><div>You will need to arrange for a shiny server to exist, and for it to allow cross-site calls from the client.  (Unless you can somehow host wordpress on your machine too - does it work like that?).</div><div><br></div><div>Can glimmer server accept cross-site calls?</div><div><br></div><div>-Alex </div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br><br>On Tuesday, March 5, 2013 8:31:05 AM UTC-8, brendan dornan wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34);font-size:16px;line-height:24px\">Great package, thanks for building. Is it possible to render interactive charts in self-hosted blog posts like one can with the googleVis + R package?</span></h1><h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><br></h1><h1 style=\"font-size:x-large;background-image:none;max-width:700px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif;line-height:normal\"><a href=\"https://code.google.com/p/google-motion-charts-with-r/wiki/UsingWordPress\" style=\"font-size:16px;line-height:24px\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://code.google.com/p/google-motion-charts-with-r/wiki/UsingWordPress&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw00oGFAuD4lEPV0taYRVlCJ\">Using googleVis output with WordPress</a><br></h1><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><a href=\"http://wordpress.org/\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wordpress.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tfWlAA4YHf_N27DO3oLGC\">WordPress</a> is a popular web software for creating websites and blogs. Here we give some tips about the usage with googleVis output.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">By default WordPress does not allow JavaScript code (and hence googleVis output) to be inserted into a page. However, additional plugins allow us to extend the functions of WordPress.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">One option of embedding JavaScript code inside a WordPress post is to use the <a href=\"http://wordpress.org/extend/plugins/custom-fields-shortcode\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://wordpress.org/extend/plugins/custom-fields-shortcode&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2R08FHxAl2dYsb90Pyzjs2\">&quot;custom fields shortcode&quot;</a> plugin. This plugin allows you to create a custom field for the googleVis code, which can be referred to in your article.</p><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Suppose you created a motion chart in R:</p><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span>M </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span> gvisMotionChart</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Fruits</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Fruit&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&quot;Year&quot;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span><br>                     options</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span>list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>width</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">400</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> height</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">370</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">))</span></pre><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">Copy the chart code, e.g. from</p><pre style=\"font-size:12px;padding:0.5em;overflow:auto;font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;max-width:70em;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">print</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span>M</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span><span> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,136,0)\">&#39;chart&#39;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span></pre><p style=\"line-height:1.25em;max-width:64em;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:arial,sans-serif\">and paste it into the value text area of a custom field in WordPress, e.g. with instance name <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">Fruits</tt>. To include the motion chart into your article add <tt style=\"font-family:Monaco,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,monospace;font-size:12px;max-width:66em\">[cf]Fruits[/cf]</tt> into the post, see the figure below for an illustration. For more details see also the <a href=\"http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googleVis/vignettes/googleVis.pdf\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"color:rgb(0,0,204)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/googleVis/vignettes/googleVis.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409675310000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2syq0JK3LyUuClPwD2TQWG\">vignette</a>.</p></blockquote></div>"
